course: dictionary
lesson: 6554
title: Newton: a unit and a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. A capital letter often shows which one. «Isaac Newton» with a capital N is a person, a famous English scientist. A small n, as in «forces are measured in newtons», means a unit, a way of measuring force.
explain: Context clues help you choose the right meaning. «Forces are measured in newtons» and «a forcemeter» tell you a newton is for measuring. Like metres or kilograms, it is a unit. A forcemeter, also called a newton meter, shows how many newtons of force are pushing or pulling.
explain: Look at the words around the name too. «Isaac Newton explained that gravity makes an apple fall» tells you he was a scientist who explained things. In «Newton's cradle», the 's shows the toy is connected with him. Always check: does my meaning make sense in the sentence?
fact: A newton is the unit of force, and its symbol is N.
fact: Forces are measured in newtons, using a forcemeter, which is also called a newton meter.
fact: On Earth, 1 kg has a weight of about 10 N.
fact: Isaac Newton was a famous English scientist who explained gravity and the laws of motion.
fact: «Newton» with a capital letter is a name; the unit «newton» is written with a small letter.
exercise: What is the symbol for a newton? | m | kg | s | *N
exercise: «Isaac Newton explained that gravity makes an apple fall.» What was Isaac Newton? | A famous English footballer | A kind of fruit | *A famous English scientist | A type of rocket
exercise: Which sentence uses newtons as a unit? | *Forces are measured in newtons | Isaac Newton built an early telescope | Newton's cradle is a fun toy to watch | Newton said a falling apple made him think
test: Why does the capital N in «Isaac Newton» matter? | It shows the word is a unit of force | It shows the word is a question | It shows the name of a person | *It shows a person's name, a proper noun
test: About how many newtons does an apple weigh? | About 10 | About 100 | *About 1 | About 1000
exam: What does a forcemeter measure? | Time | Temperature | *Force, in newtons | Length
